The '''AP NFL Rookie of the Year (ROTY)''' is an annual award presented by the [[Associated Press]] (AP) to the top first-year offensive and defensive players in the [[National Football League]] (NFL). Winners are selected by a nationwide panel of 50 members of the AP who regularly cover the league.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.nfl.com/news/panthers-newton-voted-ap-offensive-rookie-of-the-year-09000d5d8269d38a |title=Panthers' Newton voted AP Offensive Rookie of the Year |work=NFL.com |agency=Associated Press |date=February 4, 2012 |access-date=January 29, 2013}}</ref> The AP has chosen an offensive rookie of the year since 1957 and a defensive rookie of the year since 1967. For the 2025 season, [[Carolina Panthers]] wide receiver [[Tetairoa McMillan]] and [[Cleveland Browns]] linebacker [[Carson Schwesinger]] were respectively named the offensive and defensive winners.

Ballots are cast at the end of the [[National Football League regular season|regular season]] and before the [[NFL playoffs|playoffs]]. Since 2011, winners of the AP Rookie of the Year awards are announced at the [[NFL Honors]] presentation the night before the [[Super Bowl]] along with other AP awards.<ref name="a">{{cite web|url=https://www.nfl.com/news/alec-baldwin-to-host-2nd-annual-nfl-honors-super-bowl-eve-0ap1000000123753 |title=Alec Baldwin to host '2nd Annual NFL Honors' Super Bowl Eve |work=NFL.com |publisher=National Football League |date=January 8, 2013 |access-date=January 29, 2013}}</ref> While several organizations recognize their own [[NFL Rookie of the Year]], the NFL considers the award given by the AP to be its official honor,<ref>{{cite news|last1=Demovsky|first1=Rob|title=Lacy is PFWA's top rookie; AP award next?|url=https://www.espn.com/blog/green-bay-packers/post/_/id/6534/lacy-is-pfwas-top-rookie-ap-award-next|access-date=April 16, 2017|work=ESPN.com|date=January 14, 2014}}</ref> with the winners listed in the league's annual ''Record and Fact Book''.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Birkett|first1=Dave|title=Lions' Ndamukong Suh: Another rookie of year|url=http://www.freep.com/article/20110118/SPORTS01/110118048//1049/sports01|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110121125655/http://www.freep.com/article/20110118/SPORTS01/110118048//1049/sports01|url-status=dead|archive-date=January 21, 2011|access-date=December 28, 2017|work=Detroit Free Press|date=January 18, 2011}}</ref>

